    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d538-a16">

                <pb facs="0894" n="758" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg758"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 16 in No.
                    973.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Samoan Chiefs to Mr. Blacklock.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Capital of Samoa, Faleula</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1888-09-09"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 9, 1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Highness</hi>: We, the chiefs and rulers of
                    Samoa, respectfully beg to notify your highness that we have this day, with
                    consent of the majority of the Samoan people, elected as a King Malietoa Tooa
                    Mataafa.</p>
                <p>Further, we wish to notify your highness that it is the desire of nearly all the
                    Samoan people that Tamasese ceases to be king of Samoa and Brandeis to have no
                    more connection with the Government and such connection ceases from this
                    day.</p>
                <p>After careful consideration we are determined to abide the action we have now
                    taken to defend our rights to elect what King we, the united people of Samoa,
                    may choose to rule over us.</p>
                <p>We feel confident that peace and good order will be maintained in Samoa, and for
                    our future guidance we wish to be allowed the privilege of selecting three
                    gentlemen representing the three great nations having commercial interests in
                    Samoa to advise us in our endeavors to rule impartially and justly.</p>
                <p>May yon live.</p>
                <p>We are the Tumua, and Pule, and Aiga, and forty others.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
